{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>When a woman vows a vow to YHWH and her father hears</b> – Scripture wished to mention the prohibition first, to state that even the young woman is included in the prohibition mentioned, that he shall not profane his word. Therefore, if her father confirmed it for her, the vow stands, but if he annulled it, it does not stand. And it says, <b>He will forgive her, for her father annulled it</b>, to state that 'He will forgive her' is said only when she transgresses after the father's annulment, not from the outset if she transgressed the vow and afterward he annulled it, as they said (Nazir 22a): he strikes down [further prohibition] like one who hews, but he does not uproot the vow from its root."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The phrase 'דְּמֵיגַז גָּיֵיז' is Aramaic (literally 'from hewing he hews'); rendered hyper-literally. The referent of 'he' in the prohibition 'shall not profane his word' is ambiguous in the source."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:09:33.379419070Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}